            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0090" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.852/54</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Erwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 861</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-13">November 13,
                        1939</date>.<lb/>[Received November 20.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I was
                    informed today by Mr. Harold Darlington, British Vice Consul in Tegucigalpa,
                    that it has been reliably reported the German freighter <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wesermunde</hi>, at present at Curaçao, West Indies, is negotiating for a
                    change of registry to the Honduran flag. The new name this vessel will take is
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Chirropo</hi>, according to this report.</p>
                <p>It is believed that the effort to change to Honduran registry at this time is
                    motivated by the fact that the ship is now in a port controlled by the Dutch and
                    that this step is being taken as protection for the German owners in the event
                    the Netherlands break relations with Germany.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John D. Erwin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
